### Personal internship report & presentation materials (not project docs) ###
# pfa.tex/pfa.pdf (ENSET/CGI internship report) and the progress-presentation
# .pptx/.docx are personal deliverables for the internship supervisor, not
# documentation of this codebase - keep them out of the public repo entirely.
# (architecture.md, stack.md, and diagrams/ remain tracked - those document
# the project itself.)
# The whole report source folder (chapters, preamble, its own imgs/ and
# built PDF) - added 2026-08-31 when pfa.tex was split into docs/pfa/.
docs/pfa/
docs/pfa.tex
docs/*.aux
docs/*.log
docs/*.out
docs/*.toc
docs/*.synctex.gz
docs/pfa.pdf
docs/*.pptx
docs/*.docx

### This project's local runtime state ###
# Every component (repository_metadata, dependency_graph, vector_index,
# doc_generator's page manifest) persists to its own caller-supplied SQLite file -
# see docs/architecture.md "Storage architecture". None of these are meant to be
# committed, whatever path/name a caller gives them.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
# Default local runtime-state directory used when indexing a repository in place
# (see src/chat_api/server.py's --metadata-db default).
# The `codepedia` CLI (019) does not use this in-repo location - its own
# state and config live under the user's home directory (~/.codepedia/),
# never inside an analyzed repository, so no separate ignore entry is needed
# for it here.
.codepedia/
# Local-only configuration/secrets (e.g. overriding the local LLM/embedding
# endpoint); nothing in this project reads a .env file today, but this project's
# local-only, no-cloud-credentials design means none should ever be committed if
# one is introduced.
.env
.env.*
*.log
